      {
        "id": "the-ticking-noise-was-not-a-tappet-it-was-low-oil-pressure",
        "title": "The ticking noise was not a tappet. It was low oil pressure.",
        "description": "The danger signal was not low oil level. It was the pump losing the ability to maintain pressure, especially at low RPM and when hot.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/1.2-ford-ranger-32-ticking-sound.png",
            "alt": "Ford Ranger 3.2 ticking sound visualisation showing 5 day countdown from first noise to engine seizure",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Monday"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Faint ticking at idle"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Audible when cold, quieter when warm, but never fully gone."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Thursday"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil light flickered"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The dipstick showed full oil, so the vehicle was driven again."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Friday"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solid oil light, knock, silence"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The engine seized within minutes on the M6."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If your 3.2 Duratorq ticks at idle or the oil pressure light flickers even once, stop driving and test oil pressure. A £50-£100 test can confirm pump failure before the bottom end seizes."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Failure timeline"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-ticking-noise-was-not-a-tappet-it-was-low-oil-pressure",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "5-000-miles-was-not-the-story-five-days-was",
        "title": "5,000 miles was not the story - five days was.",
        "description": "From first tick to seizure took less than a week. The owner assumed diesel injector or tappet noise because the oil level looked normal.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/2.2-ford-ranger-32-timeline.png",
            "alt": "Ford Ranger 3.2 timeline showing 5 days from first ticking noise to engine seizure on M6",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What the owner assumed"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "\"Probably a tappet or injector.\" Common diesel noise was assumed, not oil pressure failure."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What was actually happening"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The oil pump was failing internally. Bearings starved, the crankshaft scored, and the bottom end seized."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "\"The car still drove, but every journey sounded worse than the last.\""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Symptom 1"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Gradual loss of power over 3-4 days"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Symptom 2"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Deep rhythmic knock, louder under load"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Recovery"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Flashing oil light on the M6, then seizure"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Workshop diagnosis"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "5-000-miles-was-not-the-story-five-days-was",
          "order": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "the-oil-pump-failed-internally-the-bottom-end-starved-and-seized",
        "title": "The oil pump failed internally. The bottom end starved and seized.",
        "description": "The vehicle was recovered to a Ford specialist. The engine would not turn manually. There was no blocked pickup; the pump had simply stopped maintaining oil pressure.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.2-ford-ranger-32-oil-pump-failed.png",
            "alt": "Ford 3.2 Duratorq oil pump failure - comparison of healthy pump versus failed pump with scored gears",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.1-ford-ranger-32-seized-bearings.png",
            "alt": "Ford 3.2 Duratorq crankshaft bearings seized and welded to journals from oil pump failure",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/3.3-ford-ranger-32-scored-crankshaft.png",
            "alt": "Ford 3.2 Duratorq crankshaft scored beyond repair from oil pump failure",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil pump"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Failed internally - no oil pressure"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Crank bearings"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Seized and welded to the journals"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Conrod bearings"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Severe scoring with copper visible"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Crankshaft"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Scored beyond repair"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Turbocharger"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Unknown condition due to likely oil starvation damage"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil pickup"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Clean - no blockage found"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Specialist verdict"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "\"The oil pump failed internally. It stopped pumping oil. The bottom end starved, and the crankshaft seized. There's nothing rebuildable here.\""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Replacement options"
          }
        ],
