      {
        "id": "the-engine-was-replaced-but-the-turbo-had-also-run-without-oil",
        "title": "The engine was replaced, but the turbo had also run without oil.",
        "description": "When the oil pump fails, every component relying on oil pressure is at risk. The turbo could fail weeks or months after the replacement engine is fitted.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Path A - chosen"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Fit only the used engine and risk the existing turbo."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£3,800"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If turbo fails later: add £800-£1,200 plus labour. Kept upfront cost down but left a known risk."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Path B"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Replace the turbo preventatively at the same time as the engine."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£4,500"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£3,800 engine + ~£700 turbo. Eliminates the risk entirely."
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/5.1-ford-ranger-32-turbo-oil-starvation.png",
